[length:05:12]
[ti:The cage]
[ar:Aracne]
[al:Chaotic-Disfuntyonal]
[au:Aracne]
[lr:Aracne]
[by:Aracne]
[re:LRC Workbench by Azaria (lrc-workbench.azariadev.dev)]
[ve:0.3.2]
[00:04.35]I remember...
[00:10.07]learning silence...
[00:17.18]I remember...
[00:23.00]being afraid of sound...
[00:58.46]I learned your footsteps like a warning,
[01:01.76]read your breathing like a storm,
[01:04.93]watched your eyes for signs of thunder,
[01:08.05]learned to shrink and call it warmth.
[01:11.21]I thanked you when the shouting ended,
[01:14.65]called the quiet “love” and “peace”,
[01:17.81]held my body like a hostage
[01:21.20]praying rage would fall asleep.
[01:24.45]You never needed chains to keep me,
[01:27.90]never needed fists to bruise
[01:31.11]you only made the whole world smaller
[01:34.46]until there was no place to move.
[01:39.55]Every exit felt like the wrong choice
[01:42.16]Every silence sounded like your voice
[01:45.47]You called it love - it tasted like fear
[01:48.71]You built a cage and moved inside me
[01:52.12]You made me thank you for surviving
[01:55.32]Made me beg for scraps of calm
[01:58.49]Taught my shaking hands to call it healing
[02:01.77]while you taught my heart alarm
[02:18.19]I walked on glass you could not see,
[02:21.21]smiled wide with bleeding feet,
[02:24.56]measured every word for danger,
[02:27.31]made myself careful, soft, discreet.
[02:31.11]You broke the room with sudden weather,
[02:33.61]then wept and held me like a child,
[02:36.95]said the wound was proof you loved me,
[02:40.18]said your chaos made me wild.
[02:43.76]Every boundary felt like violence,
[02:46.81]every “no” became a fight,
[02:50.15]I stopped trusting my own memory
[02:53.56]just to make it through the night.
[02:58.15]Every exit felt like the wrong choice
[03:01.20]Every silence sounded like your voice
[03:04.63]You called it love - it tasted like fear
[03:07.61]You built a cage and moved inside me
[03:10.95]You made me thank you for surviving
[03:14.40]Made me beg for scraps of calm
[03:17.35]Taught my shaking hands to call it healing
[03:21.21]while you taught my heart alarm
[03:24.83]I flinch at kindness.
[03:27.68]I brace for doors.
[03:30.93]I still hear thunder
[03:34.11]in harmless storms.
[03:37.53]And somewhere now
[03:40.63]someone believes
[03:44.01]your gentle hands
[03:47.73]mean safety.
[03:51.58]I survived you.
[03:54.48]I don't know if they will.
[03:58.80]There will be others after me
[04:04.47]and that is what still breaks me.
[04:10.35]God...
[04:12.05]keep them safe...
[04:15.10]...from you.
[04:19.54]Every exit felt like the wrong choice
[04:22.55]Every silence sounded like your voice
[04:25.60]You called it love - it tasted like fear
[04:28.81]You built a cage but i'm still here
[04:32.12]You made me kneel,
[04:33.52]you made me bleed,
[04:35.50]you taught my bones to live in dread
[04:38.62]but something fierce survived in me
[04:41.44]that would not die,
[04:43.02]that would not bend.
[04:51.32]You taught me how to kneel...
[04:56.79]Now watch me stand.
[05:02.49]without you
